[33.794551, "o", "\u001b[29A\u001b[1G\u001b[K  \u001b[2mv0.7.4\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Provider: anthropic-vertex\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Model: claude-haiku-4-5\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Working directory: /tmp/ami-demo-IFNc4e\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Session: session-20261113-135051-374-0\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[4G\u001b[K\u001b[90mermissions: auto-allow\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[90mTip: Run \u001b[1mami --skill <name>\u001b[22m to pin a skill stance for the session.\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m\u2298 Indexing skipped: no project root found\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[E\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255m > Create a Python script maze.py that generates a random 21\u00d721 maze using recursive backtracking, \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mthen solves it from top-left to bottom-right using BFS, and prints the maze to the terminal with \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mwalls as \u2588, open paths as spaces, and the solution path marked with \u00b7 in green (ANSI colors). Use a \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mfixed seed of 42 for reproducibility. Run it. \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[KI'll create a maze generator and solver with visualization. Let me build this step by step.\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m[Checkpoint cp-1794574284425-1: /tmp/ami-demo-IFNc4e/maze.py]\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K  \u001b[38;5;167m\u25cf\u001b[39m \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;167mfile_edit\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\u001b[2m \u00b7 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;243m/tmp/ami-demo-IFNc4e/maze.py\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;167m\u001b[39mfile_edit /tmp/ami-demo-IFNc4e/maze.py \u001b[2m4.2s\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[E\u001b[E\u001b[1G\u001b[K\